"e27df00f-7404-5963-a875-5f57e801702e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107324} :answer-field/id #uuid "d078c165-bd3b-5097-be93-c04451228952" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107321}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d5df118a-6629-591e-bac9-243a7536e271" :question/math-academy-id "q-13445" :question/problem "![](images/36/36ea34524b2ca277e8061441492711d36c8065e765d519d85d4008da97c3f8b3.png)\n\nConsider the figure shown above. Which of the following triplets of points are collinear?\n\nI. $M,N,R$\n\nII. $P,S,T$\n\nIII. $O,P,S$" :question/worked-solution "- $M,N,R$ are collinear since there is a straight line that passes through all of them.\n\n![](images/b8/b8fae613772422b14fce2e2db0762f659599f0b17409223ec291802b5d760d9c.png)\n\n- $P,S,T$ are **not** collinear since we can't draw a straight line that passes through all of them.\n\n![](images/85/85638c1466360f3e5285c34e84903824140b9e2fc72a0f029ab1ded170b64eb2.png)\n\n- $O,P,S$ are collinear since there is a straight line that passes through all of them.\n\n![](images/4b/4b7ef30e306e3c7e70dadb1524e1f60a9ea01832215009ef2ea8344cb07e7297.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110928 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110675 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9ef4e321-841e-5933-b5e4-ff7dab6c5275" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Collinear Points on a Grid" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049892 :topic/math-academy-id 1500 :topic/title "Collinear Points"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c40dda1-5408-53b5-a9ae-ec9e55f35833" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :