only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107467} {:answer/id #uuid "269504ce-2a6a-5ccd-9cf4-5b401742671b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107468} {:answer/id #uuid "5b210728-6a80-5b8f-97a2-05caf904c89a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107469} {:answer/id #uuid "7ddee60b-d64d-5874-a34e-03b6baff8ee0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107470}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "269504ce-2a6a-5ccd-9cf4-5b401742671b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107468} :answer-field/id #uuid "e907c4ba-8343-5fdd-abfe-8b39f70e8112" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107465}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4ea9e0d7-7c8f-5224-8f6f-e5c31c36ab4a" :question/math-academy-id "q-155503" :question/problem "![](images/bb/bb96a7692787ca6e055b41d4f1599b87baa1ea331544ea42235a7131343c76e3.png)\n\nWhich of the diagrams above shows three collinear points?" :question/worked-solution "Three (or more) points are collinear if a straight line passes through all points.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our diagrams in turn.\n\n- Diagram I shows three collinear points. There is a straight line that passes through all three of these points.\n\n![](images/54/54735541d4dfc424fe186ddabe0c3f9d3cbd45a0dc7a1b8f4551cf8c5e5bc14f.png)\n\n- Diagram II shows three points that are *not* collinear. We can't draw a straight line that passes through all three points.\n\n![](images/f0/f00f882c97fd201178e54f29151a48a4f41d4108cf375104cc338e968c55761b.png)\n\n- Diagram III shows three collinear points. There is a straight line that passes through all three of these points.\n\n![](images/6e/6e0c0320775d93364e32655d1e09081382078fa7e96fbe621a8c558f63dfcabb.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110930 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110735 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f8a6ac29-44ee-5305-be7a-41f9ae742756" :knowledge-point/title "Plotting a Vertically Compressed Exponential Growth Function" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048789 :topic/math-academy-id 1530 :topic/title "Graphing Exponential Growth Functions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ccd936dc-2ce3-5688-b56a-b0ecc37f257e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107472} {:answer/id #uuid "20250a95-7a58-50a2-86af-ac75707f5323" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107473} {:answer/id #uuid "425ef207-4465-55fb-b916-bb50e95c3ce5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107474} {:answer/id #uuid "4c919938-5471-5d61-a615-93a4783683e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107475} {:answer/id #uuid "64d5485a-0b3b-5a3a-897b-2ac54cc10627" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107476}] :answer-field/id #uuid "6e137d62-178c-54b4-8967-9073e2828a76" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107471}] :question/id #uuid "afce8b19-fb25-5544-97f9-8f9caa8b68b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-166992" :question/problem "Which of the following statements ar