\n2. $AC^(―)≅AB^(―)$\n3. $AC = 3cm$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111260 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110776 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "00889b75-3745-52f6-9157-912846482689" :knowledge-point/title "Describing a Quadrilateral" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049068 :topic/math-academy-id 1459 :topic/title "Classifying Quadrilaterals"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aaeafc54-7b92-5062-9bdb-15d818ddc76e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186109286} {:answer/id #uuid "e459090c-5c9d-5d00-95e2-d581d6447dc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186109287} {:answer/id #uuid "e6d9a4f1-68e6-5d47-8c82-5c0b4c9aa084" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186109288} {:answer/id #uuid "35964d8d-753e-5e39-9f1d-9b0c320a166c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186109289} {:answer/id #uuid "6bdd5188-95f9-5c2b-b965-cff6cf0912dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186109290}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e459090c-5c9d-5d00-95e2-d581d6447dc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186109287} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a5fa196-47ec-5e14-99ea-eb0655130b41" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186109285}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "599179be-ddc2-50ab-a431-64168ebbcf12" :question/math-academy-id "q-53000" :question/problem "![](images/6b/6bffbc53c9e35da03655638ca40c5899bc5290cbadf3d14aef8e82585f14e004.png)\n\nWhich of the following terms describe the shape above?\n\nI. Kite\n\nII. Rectangle\n\nIII. Trapezoid" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the hierarchy diagram of quadrilaterals, where each shape below another is a specific type of the one above it.\n\n![](images/1d/1dbe4c3e8ea97c0ac077c37143802366c5817d86965ab1dbc5abf54cd01d27c3.png)\n\nLet's now look at the terms one by one.\n\n- The given figure is a quadrilateral with two pairs of congruent sides that are adjacent to each other, so it is a kite.\n\n- Since the four angles of the quadrilateral are right angles, it is a rectangle.\n\n- The quadrilateral has two pairs of opposite sides that are parallel to each other, not one pair. So it is **not** a trapezoid.\n\nConsequently, the given shape is described by terms I (kite), and II (rectangle)."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111261 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110776 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "00889b75-3745-52f6-9157-912846482689" :knowledge-point/title "Describing a Quadrilateral" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049068 :topic/math-academy-id 1459 :topic/title "Classifying Quadrilaterals"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "921a8f62-7b9e-5a71-a864-a226f63904a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186109292} {:answer/id #uuid "04d5d273-2e8c-574c-9ec8-183aa79e27a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186109293} {:answer/id #uuid "136bf9e7-1089-50ee-8ebc-d7fd4c0afd45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186109294} {:answer/id #uuid "41f2a6b0-f578-52da-97ed-f091213a4bd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.ty