98-b35a-5246353f9baa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186109302}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc9f265f-b2fd-5a80-9c41-ff41fc5c7c0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186109298} :answer-field/id #uuid "e187a24b-d5d5-548e-a10f-715cef7faf9c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186109297}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5c9c084b-0547-549b-b2ae-ba90597387ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-53010" :question/problem "![](images/b6/b68f8d3d0634999697051b668c06dd34c1191905a7bebda79925cd437d454d36.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the trapezoid above?\n\nI. $\\overset{―}{AB}∥\\overset{―}{CD}.$\n\nII. $m∠ABC={90}^{∘}.$\n\nIII. $\\overset{―}{AD}∥\\overset{―}{BC}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The trapezoid has a pair of parallel sides, $\\overset{―}{AB}∥\\overset{―}{CD}.$\n\n- Statement II is true. We can see that $∠ABC$ is a right angle, that is, $m∠ABC={90}^{∘}.$\n\n- Statement III is false. The trapezoid has one pair of parallel sides, $\\overset{―}{AB}∥\\overset{―}{CD}.$ We can see that $\\overset{―}{AD}$ and $\\overset{―}{BC}$ are not parallel.\n\nIn conclusion, statements I and II are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111263 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110777 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c81cf5ed-8dd7-5174-b8e9-faf63bf0a278" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Quadrilateral" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049068 :topic/math-academy-id 1459 :topic/title "Classifying Quadrilaterals"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8113f0c1-13bf-5ab2-9